{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/884795-what-are-the-best-ban-s-and-bane-s-you-ve-created","id":884795,"title":"What are the best ban's and bane's you've created.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-07T12:02:02-07:00","id":884795,"title":"What are the best ban's and bane's you've created.","content":"Following the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues\">vein of the Virtue and Vice thread</a>, what are the most interesting, or played out well Ban's and Bane's you've created?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:31:55-07:00","id":884856,"title":"","content":"Had a rank 3 Walmart spirit called Maw-Mart, it's Ban meant that he had to alter the prices of anything on it's shop to a lower one if presented a receipt for a cheaper price from another place. The Bane was said objects.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could cheat it by making an arbitrary receipt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:09:26-07:00","id":884892,"title":"","content":"For a ghost that from a drowning victim their ban was that they couldn't cross over water (like the vampire myth) while their bane was an item soaked in the lake they died in for a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:29:01-07:00","id":884909,"title":"","content":"Spirit of Seriousness, antagonistic to the Spirit of Comedy the party allied themselves with.<br /> Ban: Cannot materialize within a mile from a succesfull attempt at black humour.<br /> Bane: Office supplies that were previously used in a gag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:31:31-07:00","id":884948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/884795-what-are-the-best-ban-s-and-bane-s-you-ve-created?p=884909#post884909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit of Seriousness, antagonistic to the Spirit of Comedy the party allied themselves with.<br /> Ban: Cannot materialize within a mile from a successful attempt at black humour.<br /> Bane: Office supplies that were previously used in a gag.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ironically enough, this spirit sounds pretty funny to me. What did it look like? You chose a mile because of the &quot;walk a mile in their shoes&quot; expression, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:23:09-07:00","id":885420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/884795-what-are-the-best-ban-s-and-bane-s-you-ve-created?p=884948#post884948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ironically enough, this spirit sounds pretty funny to me. What did it look like? You chose a mile because of the &quot;walk a mile in their shoes&quot; expression, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's looks? A floating grey suit without a person inside. Or, earlier on, a floating fedora. The players found it silly. The PC's did too. The spirit was pissed at their reaction.<br /> About the mile distance, I chose it beacause of the fact that it's just big enough of a distance to be annoying, not small enough to be walk down the street, and not high enough to be downright atrocious. Also beacause it's a round neat easily managable basic number. At least when it comes to imperial units. As it was though, metric spirits didn't have that fun existances. I wasn't even aware of the expression after the fact, but it made for a nice touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:49:52-07:00","id":886513,"title":"","content":"I've used bans and banes for True Fae; we had one recently called the CEO. Each aspect had a different ban/bane, plus a couple universal ones:<br /> <br /> Ice Queen: calculating woman in a skirted power suit, represented Ruthlessness. Bane: fire. Ban: the laughter of children.<br /> Dad Boss: overly-friendly golf buddy, represented Congeniality. Bane: red things (red tape). Ban: had to compete in any game he was challenged to.<br /> Golden Boy: young man with perfect dress and hair, represented Nepotism. Bane: silver-backed mirrors. Ban: must obey anyone of higher authority than him.<br /> Fat Cat: anthropomorphic obese feline in a suit, represented Greed. Bane: laser pointers. Ban: must eat any food offered to it.<br /> Monster Boss: terrifying creature of of horns, bone, and fur, represented Power. Bane: rodents. Ban: cannot harm living creatures.<br /> Universal bane: church bells. Universal bane: their own tie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:36:09-07:00","id":891233,"title":"","content":"One Ban I had fun with was for a Helion that led the local choir of such in a Miami-set 1e campaign. During the evenings when he was somewhat less powerful he would tend to wander around among the Mundanes using Mortal Mask to inform himself on the state of the mortals Below. He'd also ended up adopting a couple of the local mages, so he'd check on them now and again.<br /> <br /> His Ban while in this lessened state was that he couldn't cross through an opaque entryway (non-glass door, etc) without someone opening the door for him. This led to some amusement in one particular scene I can recall, where he was talking with one of said mages in her apartment and when it was time for him to leave he stared at her door for a long moment until she came around and opened it for him","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:44:29-07:00","id":892501,"title":"","content":"A powerful spirit of birth and rebirth.<br /> Ban: Has to spend a willpower if they want to attack someone who has given birth to a child.<br /> Bane: Any weapon wielded by someone who was not born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:39:03-07:00","id":892614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/884795-what-are-the-best-ban-s-and-bane-s-you-ve-created?p=892501#post892501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bane: Any weapon wielded by someone who was not born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you clarify this one? I can see it as either too common (Cesareans are quite common in the USA, at least), or exceedingly rare. Would all Prometheans or Demons count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T12:12:53-07:00","id":892687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/884795-what-are-the-best-ban-s-and-bane-s-you-ve-created?p=892614#post892614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you clarify this one? I can see it as either too common (Cesareans are quite common in the USA, at least), or exceedingly rare. Would all Prometheans or Demons count?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The original intent was Prometheans/Demons or like, a robot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}